# Context shim (see meta.json): NOT the real (1208-line)
# altunelyusuf/SemanticTechnologies@bad0fa7c46
# landscape/01-research/semtech_research_v6_8_0.ttl -- a minimal stand-in.
# This region never reads g1's pre-existing triples, only adds to it, so a
# few placeholder triples are enough to make the Graph().parse(...) call in
# the captured context real. The prefix declarations, however, ARE the real
# file's (its lines 1-10, verbatim): g1 keeps them as bindings, the
# repository serialises g1 (build_core_v6_9_0.py:120), and `@graph g1` adds
# the block's own prefixes to it -- the driver checks that none of these is
# lost. Identical for both representations.
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix prov: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix res: <http://example.org/rdodi/research-ontology#> .
@prefix schema: <https://schema.org/> .
@prefix semtech: <http://example.org/semtech#> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix sr: <http://example.org/semtech/research#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

sr:ResearchCorpus a sr:Corpus ;
    sr:placeholder "pre-existing content, unrelated to this region" .
